WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Cybersecurity professionals regularly make decisions under uncertainty.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.332
Threat intelligence analysts evaluate competing explanations.

3
00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:12.682
SOC analysts determine whether alerts represent malicious activity.

4
00:00:12.682 --> 00:00:21.991
Incident responders interpret incomplete evidence, risk teams assess future scenarios, and managers decide how to prioritize limited resources.

5
00:00:21.991 --> 00:00:24.895
Structured techniques can support all of these activities.

6
00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:32.887
SATs help teams document assumptions, compare explanations, identify useful indicators, and communicate confidence.

7
00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:35.811
They make reasoning easier to review and improve.

8
00:00:35.811 --> 00:00:39.024
Structured techniques do not replace technical expertise.

9
00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:46.786
They support evidence-based decision-making when technical facts, operational context, and uncertainty must be considered together.
